{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Generate Monthly Report",
  "description": "Automatically sets config.ini to last month's date range, runs the report generator, and summarises the output with narrative commentary on the key figures.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Generate the monthly hospital report. Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. Calculate last month's date range (first day to last day of the previous calendar month from today's date).\n2. Update config.ini — set start_date and end_date under [report] to those dates.\n3. Run the report: execute `python3 generate_report.py` in the workspace root.\n4. Read the terminal output. If it succeeded, report the output file path.\n5. Based on the printed figures (registered patients, returning patients, revenue, duplicates), write a short 2-3 sentence narrative commentary interpreting what the numbers mean — e.g. whether registrations grew or fell vs the previous period, whether revenue was strong, whether duplicates need attention. Keep it factual and concise."
  }
}